Skia: "[graphite] Include hairline and subpixel strokes in inflation radius"
(Skia bug 577352772; no CVE listed yet): Graphite's ClipStack computed draw
bounds that could be too small for hairlines and strokes thinner than a
pixel, so their rendering could reach past the bounds used for clipping.
Not described as a security fix; carried as GPU rendering robustness,
cherry-picked by Skia to every Stable milestone. Skia main commit
0b6488a8123559cb72c03b987c2d717047bcac21, cut down to the ClipStack part for
older milestones and merged on 2026-10-30 to chrome/m157
(ca84ce0a6f1659748188469a89361ccea71e3a64) and m158; the m156 merge (Skia
Gerrit CL 1411518) was still open. This is the m157 merge, at third_party/skia.
Drop it once a 157 tag's Skia has it.

